      x = 0.0000: bracket threshold (y^2+2y)/(y^2+1) = 1.500000
      x = 0.3000: bracket threshold (y^2+2y)/(y^2+1) = 1.594796
      x = 0.6180: bracket threshold (y^2+2y)/(y^2+1) = 1.618034
      x = 1.0000: bracket threshold (y^2+2y)/(y^2+1) = 1.600000
      x = 2.0000: bracket threshold (y^2+2y)/(y^2+1) = 1.500000
      independent of rho = 2^L/M_0: the golden value is the optimum of the construction, not of the number.
  VERDICT PHI2: four knobs, four different responses (universal / special / class-dependent / construction-
  dependent).  No parameter moves the AMM and Collatz golden values together: across programs the shared phi
  is NUMEROLOGY (common algebra of the smallest hyperbolic unit), inside AMM it is one mechanism with three faces.
