====================================================================================================
AD1  adelic radii: Polya-Bertrandias needs sum_v log R_v > 0
====================================================================================================
  Bernstein series of a parity word w with odd-step positions d_1 < d_2 < ...:
    (i)  g_w(Y) = sum_l 2^(d_l) Y^l in Z[[Y]]:      log2 R_inf = -limsup d_l/l,  log2 R_2 = +liminf d_l/l
    (ii) f_w(X) = sum_l X^(d_l) 3^(-l) in Z[1/3][[X]]: log3 R_inf = liminf l/d_l, log3 R_3 = -limsup l/d_l
  Each term is an S-unit (S = {inf, 2, 3}), so the product formula forces sum_v log R_v = liminf - limsup <= 0.
  word                                                liminf d/l  limsup d/l  sum_v log2 R_v (i)
  Sturmian golden slope                                  2.61799     2.61805            -0.00005
  Sturmian slope log_3 2 (critical)                      1.58496     1.58499            -0.00003
  square-swap Y (1^9 0 / 1^8 0 1)                        1.11109     1.11111            -0.00002
  cube-swap Y3                                           1.11109     1.11111            -0.00002
  i.i.d. fair bits                                       1.98656     1.99904            -0.01248
  Bernoulli blocks of density 0.3/0.8 (no density)       1.42839     1.96038            -0.53198
  theta(rho) = sum_k rho^(k^2) as a function of rho: integer coefficients, R_v = 1 at every place -> sum 0.
  AMM lacunary class phi = poly + sum_j eps_j w^(2^j): R_inf = 1 (natural boundary), R_p = 1 -> sum 0.
  AMM Theorem A: phi continues to W_gamma (not a disk); the archimedean term becomes log R(W_gamma,0) =
  Lambda(gamma) > 0 for gamma < 0.3775 (THM-4467).  CONTINUATION beyond the circle of convergence is the whole
  gain; Collatz-type series are lacunary on their circle of convergence and have no continuation.
  VERDICT AD1: the engine 'integrality + smallness => vanishing' is shared (REAL), but its adelic-capacity form
  is exactly critical (sum = 0) for every Collatz function form, so it cannot carry PC; Collatz must use
  value-level inputs (Liouville/Pade/Subspace), which is what Theorems R, S, D, Y do.
