BR1  LRC small clocks from the THM-4447 capacity rule, as a function of runners n and tails r
====================================================================================================
  n runners (n-1 speeds), arc ||.|| < 1/n, bad fraction 1/a with a = n/2; a primitive row = pack of
  n-1-r speeds with gcd c, plus r tails; clock c closes if for every admissible tail signature some divisor
  d > 1 of c has sum over non-absorbed tails of g ceil(d/(a g)) < d (THM-4447 (11); base case LRC(n-1)).
    n=10 (a= 5) r=2: open clocks c <= 60: [2]
    n=10 (a= 5) r=3: open clocks c <= 60: [2, 3, 4, 6]
